  "description": "Schur-Weyl-style block decomposition probe for V_(3,2,1) at mpmath 50 dps. Two analyses: (§1) bar-pair structure of M = ρ(β_EW Δ_I^minimal) — verifies all 16 eigenvalues form 8 perfect bar-pairs with sign −1 (anti-self-reciprocal spectrum: closed under x↦−1/x); det(M) = +1. (§2) next-order correction fit — given the empirical residual = CODATA cot θ_W / (top/2nd) and the leading q^(1/5) approximation from rem:staircase-ew-k3-mpfr-finding, fits residual = q^(1/5) · (1 + α·X) for X ∈ {h, h², h³, h⁴, ℏ_q, ℏ_q², ℏ_q³} and reports α plus any small-denom rational match. Complements rem:staircase-ew-k3-mpfr-finding by searching for the structural origin of the 0.15 % residual. (Note: a direct bar-involution operator B on the SYT basis requires the Schützenberger jeu-de-taquin algorithm — not implemented here; the spectral symmetry is observed directly via the reciprocity check.)",
